---
// Generated from THREAT_MODEL.md (PRD §11.1, TRD §10.2) — Light Ribbon theme, AC-P14-07
import '../styles/theme.css';
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
  <title>Threat Model — Tether</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
    h2 {
      color: var(--t-text-900);
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    h3 {
      color: var(--t-text-900);
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    p, li {
      color: var(--t-text-700);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .threat-card {
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .badge {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      background: var(--t-blue-tint);
      color: var(--t-blue-fg);
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Threat Model &amp; Security Architecture</h1>
    <p>Tether is architected specifically to defeat the "PleaseFix" attack class demonstrated across commercial browser agents at Black Hat 2026.</p>

    <div class="t-card threat-card">
      <span class="badge">SEC-01</span>
      <h3>Indirect Prompt Injection</h3>
      <p><strong>Control:</strong> Untrusted page data tagged <code>trust: "untrusted"</code>. High-risk actions gated behind confirmation diffs (HR-8).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="t-card threat-card">
      <span class="badge">SEC-02</span>
      <h3>Confused Deputy Across Origins</h3>
      <p><strong>Control:</strong> Default deny on sensitive categories (banking, healthcare, government, auth). Strict frame boundary checks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="t-card threat-card">
      <span class="badge">SEC-03</span>
      <h3>Arbitrary JavaScript Execution</h3>
      <p><strong>Control:</strong> Complete absence of <code>evaluate_script</code> or <code>eval</code>. Prohibited by CI gate and Hard Rule 1.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="t-card threat-card">
      <span class="badge">SEC-05</span>
      <h3>Secret Leakage into Model Context</h3>
      <p><strong>Control:</strong> Mandatory outbound redaction for PANs, emails, API keys, IBANs. Zero secrets in model context (HR-7).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="t-card threat-card">
      <span class="badge">SEC-08</span>
      <h3>Relay Compromise &amp; Man-in-the-Middle</h3>
      <p><strong>Control:</strong> End-to-end encrypted envelope (X25519 ECDH + AES-256-GCM). Single point of policy: relay cannot grant capabilities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
